etween takes she'd often beat on a  punching bag there was also another time  when you were punching me in between  except for that time that she used rob  as a punching bag instead her reasoning  was pretty fair it's because we were  starting in the middle of a fight  fortunately pattinson didn't have it as  bad as another cast member that kravitz  did some serious damage to hit i hit  someone in the face like that  yikes this catwoman has some serious  claws you're fine you're batman  number four  when will the cowl struggles end  even after so many brilliant actors have  played batman the helmet portion of the  suit still causes endless suffering to  the caped crusaders that was the one  that was very very tight on my ears as  if that and the fact that he couldn't  really see wasn't enough pattinson was  also hooked up with an earpiece that he  couldn't remove himself it was a decent  idea as matt reeves was able to give the  actor clear directions when in the bat  suit but every now and then all the  walkie-talkies would wind up on the same  channel and pattinson would get a big  convoluted and very loud earful  trying to do a scene  number five this actor had a right to be  nervous  colin farrell looks tough as can be as  the penguin but racing down the street  in a speeding car was a definite cause  for alarm the actor was pretty honest  about his feelings surrounding filming  the stunt i was scared a terrified man  because i was being thrown all over the  place and they had a driver on the roof  of the car i wasn't even in control he  wasn't in control of the car at all and  had to deal with being bumped  erratically around the whole time it was  far from an easy shoot but it made the  whole acting scared portion a total  breeze  number six  you gotta work with what you've got and  in this case it was a bit of a match  made in heaven andy circus as alfred was  pretty perfect casting for a few reasons  one of them being the fact that director  matt reeves had 